{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere","id":1034495,"title":"Soul - A Subjective/Fuel Stat for the Tremere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-19T03:02:29-08:00","id":1034495,"title":"Soul - A Subjective/Fuel Stat for the Tremere","content":"Heavily inspired by David's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria\">Admonitoria</a>, and prompted by Satchel's own experimentations with the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032485-mystery-fae-warlocks-of-arcadia-crossover-template-brainstorming\">Fae Warlocks of Arcadia</a>, I started working on some homebrew for one of my own mage games recently. It's a re-imagining of the Tremere to make them Mage/Vampire hybrids, and falls somewhere between their early existence as Breath Drinkers and their formation as a Nameless Order of definitely-not-undead Mages.<br /> <br /> I've actually got it in a roughly finished state, but the most important section is their replacement subjective stat: Soul. I'd like some feedback on this. It's meant to be closer to Satiety from Beast than either Humanity or Wisdom - dots can be spent to achieve powerful effects, but burning through it too fast can have grave consequences.<br /> <br /> Soul is reset to 5/7/10 by attaching a new Soul, either through Death Magic or pseudo-diablerie via Breath Drinking.<br /> <a href=\"http://docs.google.com/document/d/17uW1ophtRO869vFkFcoF3OY3mv5VsED5PINoF_V6ZGc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">So, here it is.</a> Let me know what you think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T04:31:58-08:00","id":1034520,"title":"","content":"So this would be more like a seperate supernatural being, interesting but it would remove them as a mage, wouldn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T04:43:08-08:00","id":1034524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034520#post1034520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this would be more like a seperate supernatural being, interesting but it would remove them as a mage, wouldn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It works similarly to the Admonitoria that I linked, which are simultaneously Vampires and Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T05:09:35-08:00","id":1034527,"title":"","content":"Ok, so if the Tremere was in a vampire setting he would count as a vampire, in a mage setting count as a mage. Soul would be replace wis dominated in in a mage setting and humanity in a vampire setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T05:39:42-08:00","id":1034533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034527#post1034527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so if the Tremere was in a vampire setting he would count as a vampire, in a mage setting count as a mage. Soul would be replace wis dominated in in a mage setting and humanity in a vampire setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's simultaneously considered both a Vampire and Mage, with access to some abilities from both. This section is just about their Subjective/Fuel stat, which is Soul. It never uses Humanity or Wisdom at all. It's a crossover splat.<br /> <br /> If you haven't read over the link to David Hill's project, you should take a look. It explains the hybrid splat thing much better than I can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T06:21:20-08:00","id":1034550,"title":"","content":"When will we see the other sections, the one about their Gnosis/Blood Potency and ArcanumDisciplines? Interesting work so far, butI would note them lacking breaking points put them outside the mechanical affects of horror within the setting, and this is a horror game thus making them suitable as unfeeling antagonists not horrified protagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T06:43:07-08:00","id":1034559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034550#post1034550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When will we see the other sections, the one about their Gnosis/Blood Potency and ArcanumDisciplines? Interesting work so far, butI would note them lacking breaking points put them outside the mechanical affects of horror within the setting, and this is a horror game thus making them suitable as unfeeling antagonists not horrified protagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's mostly because Satiety (which I modeled this trait after) also lacks breaking points, and this fills a similar role - it's designed to simulate their 'hunger' for souls, which is what their existence has essentially been reduced to, much like a Beast's primary concern is their own hunger. It seems appropriate.<br /> <br /> Satiety does have other balancing mechanics, though - namely Satiety Conditions.<br /> <br /> I might add breaking points back - it'd be easy enough, and it'd be one more thing that will wear down the Soul Rating besides just choosing to spend it / passage of time, which is good. The end goal is to have souls last a fair amount of time during period of inactivity, while being able to burn through them quickly when the Tremere needs to get shit done <i>now</i>.<br /> <br /> That said, the Tremere are beings that literally lack a Soul of their own, and survive by stealing those of others. I don't want Degeneration/Detachment mechanics to play a central role at all. It should be <i>all</i> about the Soul, and making it last as long as it can (or abusing it for power).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T07:44:30-08:00","id":1034597,"title":"","content":"I think this is a good start. Myself, I like seeing the Tremere inherit some of the vampirism that they sold their souls for; if I were you, I'd write my own little background for the Tremere for this, so that any future writing you do remains consistent with your idea (and are explicable from it), despite whatever changes the devs decide to have follow.<br /> <br /> I'd also go further to distinguish them from vampires. The Tremere are more Awakened than Kindred and, even then, they should have a more unique flavour than &quot;Mages who are also Kindred&quot;. Instead of carte blanche applying the banes of vamps to a wizard, why not distill them down a bit? Focus on one to three banes and settle them into a lens you like.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T07:46:00-08:00","id":1034598,"title":"","content":"I have read the article and understand the concept. The issue that I am having is that once you change it from Wisdom, or Humanity in the case of the vampire, you are no longer playing that type of supernatural. Wisdom governs Mages, without a wisdom they are not a Mage. If the soul stat isn't subjected to the same trials as wisdom then it can't be the same. This is my main problem with any of the hybrids. That and people tend to make them to powerful breaking the balance of the system they are in. Case in point the lack of breaking points, all of the supernatural have breaking points that is one of the game balances.<br /> <br /> This is just my opinion. I could be and probably way of base with that opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:03:35-08:00","id":1034603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034598#post1034598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have read the article and understand the concept. The issue that I am having is that once you change it from Wisdom, or Humanity in the case of the vampire, you are no longer playing that type of supernatural. Wisdom governs Mages, without a wisdom they are not a Mage. If the soul stat isn't subjected to the same trials as wisdom then it can't be the same. This is my main problem with any of the hybrids. That and people tend to make them to powerful breaking the balance of the system they are in. Case in point the lack of breaking points, all of the supernatural have breaking points that is one of the game balances.<br /> <br /> This is just my opinion. I could be and probably way of base with that opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note: Beasts don't have Breaking Points for Satiety which Soul is explicitly modeled after (despite being a Mage-Vampire hybrid).<br /> <br /> As far as the effects of Souls:<ul><li><s>How does it interact with containing Paradox, which Wisdom is used for?</s></li> <li><s>How does it interact with Banes and social modifiers, which Humanity is used for?</s></li> <li>I think it should have some Breaking points, even if minor ones. They could even serve to encourage proper &quot;etiquette&quot; among Tremere. Behavior could be a valid divisor between reckless, rapacious soul-eaters, and more conscientious immortals.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-19-2017, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:14:34-08:00","id":1034610,"title":"","content":"Ok I look forward to reading more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:36:32-08:00","id":1034624,"title":"","content":"How I read the mechanics:<br /> When you grab a new Soul it does not add to your existing score but resets your score to whatever is new Soul is.<br /> <br /> Question:<br /> Is that the correct reading?<br /> <br /> Implications I can foresee if that is correct:<br /> This creates a very short and unstable recharge cycle that is very deadly when it goes wrong, that strongly encourages waiting until the last minute to refill the soul. It'd like needing a new person's bank account in order to survive every 4-9 months assuming you do nothing fun with the money. Normal people accounts would be like mundane human, organized crime members being like Kindred, and Law Enforcement being like Mages. Even if you manage an easy way to steal those accounts, the likelihood those seeking retaliation/justice get involved is almost certain after a couple years, and definite after a couple decades. This is not like Vitae which can be seen as skimming money from an account and may go unnoticed, it leaves Soulless Husks unless you are then killing the victim. This would lead long term Tremere to be serial killers of mundane humans to avoid mystical authorities who'd notice the increase of the Soulless.<br /> <br /> Request:<br /> Please critique my analysis if I was correct in my reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-19-2017, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:41:25-08:00","id":1034627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034597#post1034597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is a good start. Myself, I like seeing the Tremere inherit some of the vampirism that they sold their souls for; if I were you, I'd write my own little background for the Tremere for this, so that any future writing you do remains consistent with your idea (and are explicable from it), despite whatever changes the devs decide to have follow.<br /> <br /> I'd also go further to distinguish them from vampires. The Tremere are more Awakened than Kindred and, even then, they should have a more unique flavour than &quot;Mages who are also Kindred&quot;. Instead of carte blanche applying the banes of vamps to a wizard, why not distill them down a bit? Focus on one to three banes and settle them into a lens you like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still working explicitly on mechanics right now, but the intent is to provide some further distinction.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mLjv5JOkadY4PenpOq00YR4YJiMkj1WbMA63wB09144/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is an example of their feeding methods. Breath Drinking is meant to be the primary source of Mana, and a way for young/inexperienced Tremere to acquire souls without delving into Death.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034603#post1034603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note: Beasts don't have Breaking Points for Satiety which Soul is explicitly modeled after (despite being a Mage-Vampire hybrid).<br /> <br /> As far as the effects of Souls:<ul><li><s>How does it interact with containing Paradox, which Wisdom is used for?</s></li> <li><s>How does it interact with Banes and social modifiers, which Humanity is used for?</s></li> <li>I think it should have some Breaking points, even if minor ones. They could even serve to encourage proper &quot;etiquette&quot; among Tremere. Behavior could be a valid divisor between reckless, rapacious soul-eaters, and more conscientious immortals.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Any suggestions for breaking points that would be in-theme with Tremere existence/culture?<br /> I'm absolutely not opposed to having them - some based on the Abyss, which is absolutely still a thing they have to contend with, would be good, for starters. I may modify and lift some from Mage.<br /> <br /> For the format of the dice roll itself, I'm considering simply rolling Soul as the Dice Pool (with modifiers). I'm thinking this would result in situations where, once the Soul has become unstable, it would start a sort of inevitable decline.<br /> <br /> I am afraid of making them <i>too</i> soul-hungry, though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:45:35-08:00","id":1034628,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Just on the implications of Soul's text, I think you should probably also dial down the advantages from both parties, as the Admonitoria did.<br /> <br /> Also, Tremere should have a bit more reliable way to sever/extract souls than Mage magic or full Diablerie.<br /> <br /> What happens if a Tremere steals Person A's soul, runs it down to 1, then severs it from themselves, re-grafts it back onto A, then steals it again? Or cycles between A and B?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:45:41-08:00","id":1034629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034624#post1034624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question:<br /> Is that the correct reading?<br /> <br /> This creates a very short and unstable recharge cycle that is very deadly when it goes wrong, that strongly encourages waiting until the last minute to refill the soul...<br /> This would lead long term Tremere to be serial killers to avoid mystical authorities who'd notice the increase of the Soulless.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct, and working as designed.<br /> <br /> This has been through zero playtesting, so it might need to be adjusted. I don't ever want the Tremere to get too comfortable with their existence - those nights ended back in the convocation where they were outed in 1099.<br /> <br /> That said, it might be overtuned to the point that it breaks verisimilitude. I'll think about this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034628#post1034628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Just on the implications of Soul's text, I think you should probably also dial down the advantages from both parties, as the Admonitoria did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Suggestions? There are some dials that have been turned that I'm not comfortable presenting yet (the formatting is still too close to David's post, and I'd like to make it my own first). For example, Tremere have no Ruling Arcana. On the vampire side, they're unable to inflict Blood Bonds, create ghouls or new vampires. I'm considering removing their access to Physical Intensity as well.<br /> <br /> One of the main issues I'm seeing right now is that there are a multitude of reasons a Mage might not want to become one of the Tremere. I'm not seeing many reasons a vampire wouldn't want to pursue it. It kind of has nothing but upsides for them. Not sure how to address that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034628#post1034628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Tremere should have a bit more reliable way to sever/extract souls than Mage magic or full Diablerie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking Diablerie that functions on mortals would be fairly reliable. Do you have any suggestions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034628#post1034628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a Tremere steals Person A's soul, runs it down to 1, then severs it from themselves, re-grafts it back onto A, then steals it again? Or cycles between A and B?</div> </div> </div> </div>I will need to clarify that once any dots of Soul have been used/spent, it is no longer a fully functional Soul for any purpose other than use by the Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-19-2017, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:54:45-08:00","id":1034636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034627#post1034627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any suggestions for breaking points that would be in-theme with Tremere existence/culture?<br /> I'm absolutely not opposed to having them - some based on the Abyss, which is absolutely still a thing they have to contend with, would be good, for starters. I may modify and lift some from Mage.<br /> <br /> For the format of the dice roll itself, I'm considering simply rolling Soul as the Dice Pool (with modifiers). I'm thinking this would result in situations where, once the Soul has become unstable, it would start a sort of inevitable decline.<br /> <br /> I am afraid of making them <i>too</i> soul-hungry, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for Breaking Points, until further elaboration on &quot;culture&quot;, perhaps just pick a few of the low Humanity and Wisdom &quot;sins&quot;? Tremere are probably inured to the higher ones, but the truly alienating actions might still have some degrading effect.<br /> <br /> Regarding Soul Degradation, maybe model it like Mummy's Decent? Instead of automatic loss, you get to roll at an interval - success is bad, and drops it by 1, failure means you keeps it, but the next time is even easier to &quot;succeed&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:57:05-08:00","id":1034637,"title":"","content":"@Inodiv Thank you for the quick reply! Didn't know if the serial killer flavor was intended, but reading your breath rules for feeding I see it was intended. Those are a very clever reuse of the Diablerie rules by the way. Small note I would include the health level loss associated with feeding listed in vampire feeding though, possibly modified as you see appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:59:59-08:00","id":1034640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034637#post1034637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Inodiv Thank you for the quick reply! Didn't know if the serial killer flavor was intended, but reading your breath rules for feeding I see it was intended. Those are a very clever reuse of the Diablerie rules by the way. Small note I would include the health level loss associated with feeding listed in vampire feeding though, possibly modified as you see appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. Diablerie seemed like the way to go for their alternate method of acquiring souls, since it's about the only thing in Vampire that interacts with them.<br /> <br /> It would be possible to play one of them without going the serial-killer route, if you have at least Death 3 before becoming one. In that case you're leaving trails of soulless thralls in your wake, though, and I'm not sure that's much better from either a Pragmatic or ethical standpoint.<br /> <br /> <b>Unrelated question:</b><br /> <br /> Does anyone have any ideas on how to make Disciplines attractive to purchase when Tremere have access to Arcana, without discounting the experience cost of Disciplines below what vampires pay for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-19-2017, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T09:05:23-08:00","id":1034643,"title":"","content":"Well, Disciplines don't risk Paradox or Quiescence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T09:22:20-08:00","id":1034650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034629#post1034629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suggestions? There are some dials that have been turned that I'm not comfortable presenting yet (the formatting is still too close to David's post, and I'd like to make it my own first). For example, Tremere have no Ruling Arcana. On the vampire side, they're unable to inflict Blood Bonds, create ghouls or new vampires. I'm considering removing their access to Physical Intensity as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.<br /> From <b>Vampires</b><br /> Get:<ul><li>Immortality (Ageless, Torpor*)</li> <li>Disciplines</li> <li>Damage reduction? (Might step on Death Armor's toes) Are they living or undead?</li> <li>Physical Intensity? (Might step on Life magic's toes)</li> </ul><br /> Don't Have:<ul><li>Blood Bonds</li> <li>&quot;Easy&quot; Replication (Embrace)</li> <li>Ghouling</li> <li>Manageable Feeding (Some Lethal vs stealing Souls)</li> <li>Sunlight vulnerability</li> <li>Beast? (No Frenzy, no Predators Auras, etc.)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> From <b>Mages</b><br /> Get:<ul><li>Arcana</li> <li>Attainments</li> <li>Mage Sight</li> </ul><br /> Don't Have<ul><li>Legacies (pretty much locked in at &quot;Tremere&quot;)</li> <li>Pattern Scouring</li> <li>Paradox Containment? (Baring using the Soul option? Would make Tremere a bit cautious about their Reaching)</li> <li>Ruling Arcana (no free magic use)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Hmm. Maybe Disciplines could be capped to decrease their abilities. Or, if going for the &quot;spell-slinging lich&quot; vibe, maybe they can't get the Physical Disciplines (and have to use magic to replicate them). Another hybridization I've seen is Discplines only, but they become much more flexible, like Arcana.<br /> <br /> Assembling this list, I wonder what a Ghoul+Proximus hybrid might be like...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034629#post1034629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the main issues I'm seeing right now is that there are a multitude of reasons a Mage might not want to become one of the Tremere. I'm not seeing many reasons a vampire wouldn't want to pursue it. It kind of has nothing but upsides for them. Not sure how to address that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soul Stealing is bit more... extreme than some blood drinking. At least some vampires can stick to animals, or deal manageable harm. Tremere cause irrepairable damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034629#post1034629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking Diablerie that functions on mortals would be fairly reliable. Do you have any suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't read that part yet. That works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034629#post1034629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will need to clarify that once any dots of Soul have been used/spent, it is no longer a fully functional Soul for any purpose other than use by the Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Kinda kills stories where someone can get their soul back from the nasty lich. Does stop feeding/regeneration exploits though.<br /> <br /> Other ideas:<ul><li>Instead of Mortal(5), Vamp(7), Mage(10), base it on Integrity/Humanity/Wisdom (making higher values more prized). Degradation reduces the value that soul can restore if returned to the source (or given to another). Tremere snack on your formerly 7 Integrity Soul down to 2? Well, you have your Soul back, but your Integrity stabilizes at 2.</li> <li>Stealing Kindred Souls lets you pick up their Disciplines or Skills (like Diablerie)</li> <li>Stealing Mage Souls lets you pick one of their Praxis, Rotes, or their Ruling Arcana (for as long as you are &quot;running&quot; that Soul)</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-19-2017, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T09:23:10-08:00","id":1034651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034640#post1034640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Unrelated question:</b><br /> <br /> Does anyone have any ideas on how to make Disciplines attractive to purchase when Tremere have access to Arcana, without discounting the experience cost of Disciplines below what vampires pay for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an easy one. Count Gnosis as half for Arcana Maximums, as an allusion to their half status as mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtA 2nd pg 86</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gnosis limits the upper limit of a mage\u2019s Arcana. A mage\u2019s highest Arcanum can be three dots at Gnosis 1, four dots at Gnosis 3, and five dots at Gnosis 5. That mage\u2019s other Arcana are limited to a maximum of two dots at Gnosis 1, three dots at Gnosis 2, four dots at Gnosis 4, and five dots at Gnosis 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many Disciples would require quite high Arcanum to accomplish the same effect (I am looking at you Protean). Also the mind powers of vampires are staggering compared to the effort required by a mage to do the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-19-2017, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T09:29:44-08:00","id":1034658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034651#post1034651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an easy one. Count Gnosis as half for Arcana Maximums, as an allusion to their half status as mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, they won't hit 4-dot Arcana until Gnosis 6, and 5-dot until Gnosis 10? And that's if they even have Ruling Arcana?<br /> For all others, they'd never hit 5-dot (since they'd need Gnosis 12).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T09:39:36-08:00","id":1034662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034650#post1034650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Kinda kills stories where someone can get their soul back from the nasty lich.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true, stories where you can get <i>a</i> soul back from the Lich (just not your own) are still possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034650#post1034650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Instead of Mortal(5), Vamp(7), Mage(10), base it on Integrity/Humanity/Wisdom (making higher values more prized). Degradation reduces the value that soul can restore if returned to the source (or given to another). Tremere snack on your formerly 7 Integrity Soul down to 2? Well, you have your Soul back, but your Integrity stabilizes at 2.</li> <li>Stealing Kindred Souls lets you pick up their Disciplines or Skills (like Diablerie)</li> <li>Stealing Mage Souls lets you pick one of their Praxis, Rotes, or their Ruling Arcana (for as long as you are &quot;running&quot; that Soul)</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I might do something like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-19-2017, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T09:42:45-08:00","id":1034665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034662#post1034662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While true, stories where you can get <i>a</i> soul back from the Lich (just not your own) are still possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tremere: &quot;Hey, what's wrong with it? It's only a little smudged. Who cares if it isn't the original - they're plug-in-play.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T09:42:45-08:00","id":1034666,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> correct, that is what I meant.<br /> <br /> <br /> All of this talk of Tremere makes me feel like sharing what I've done for my own homebrew.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=801745#post801745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Minor Template</b><br /> Minor Templates are templates which are acquired by choice and dedication. In many cases even a Non-Template without assistance can gain the template if they do what is necessary and have the proper mastery. Minor templates always have prerequisites that must be met to gain them, and may be easier for certain types of character than others to fulfill (which is how they are categorized below). Associations with a Major Template (or Human) is either Prominent or Marginal. Minor Templates with a Prominent association with a Major Template may interchangeably use that Splat's Power Source for Willpower in activating the Dread Powers granted by the Minor Template and Willpower to activate things which normally take the Splat's Power Source, and requiring only a single dot in the Skill associate with the Minor Template plus the specific Specialty listed, and members of the Major Template may universally act as Mentors to lower the skill requirements to enter the Minor Template. Minor Template which are only Marginal associated with a Major Template only benefit from the ability to interchangeably use that Splat's Power Source for Willpower in activating the Dread Powers granted by the Minor Template and Willpower to activate things which normally take the Splat's Power Source. For clarification, Humans have Willpower is their Splat Power Source.<br /> <br /> Each Minor Template which isn't exclusive to a particular Major Template gains a special type of Aspiration called a Feeding Aspiration. If being with a Minor Template doesn't fulfill their Feeding Aspiration each Month, then they cumulatively lose access to a Willpower Dot for each month they abstain. If the starving being with the Minor Template fulfills their Feeding Aspiration then they immediately regain access to the Willpower Dots they've been denied access due to abstaining from their Feeding Aspiration. Feeding Aspirations also replenish Willpower points spent instead of providing beats, exactly as they do with Horrors.<br /> <br /> Minor Templates may or may not have a Bane and/or Ban, which are in place along with the severity of their Feeding Aspiration to balance them against other Minor Templates in terms of unequal Dread Powers.<br /> <br /> Each Minor Template is keyed to a Skill and a specific Specialization. The Specialization is non-negotiable, but the levels of skill needed vary depending if it is Prominently Associated with a Major Template, members of the Associated Template (or Human) only require 1 dot in the skill, those apprentice under a Mentor of the Major Template with a Prominent association require 2 dots, apprenticing under an existing Member of the Minor Template which doesn't qualify for the Prominent discount is 3 dots, and those without any guidance or innate Template association require 4 dots.<br /> <br /> Lesser Templates from World of Darkness have been revised and put together into a category with Bloodlines, Lodges, Legacies, and Entitlements to form the general grouping of Minor Templates. Some lesser templates have been cut from the list and replaced by thematically appropriate equivalents, like bloodbathers replace ghouls. skinchangers replace wolfblooded, Miracle-Worker and Mad Scientists have replaced sleepwalkers and thaumaturges, and goblins replaces ensorsocelled and fae touch. Body thieves are connected to sin-eaters as ghouls used to be connected to vampires, sleepwalker used to be connected to mages, and wolfblooded used to be connected to Uratha.Hunter is a new Minor Template which is horrified and infuriated by predication upon and atrocities against ensoulled beings and who dedicate themselves, mind/body/soul, to hunt monsters. The minor templates have been converted available Chronicles of Darkness mechanics, which has greatly simplified and streamlined.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Mage Associated</span> Template Medicine (Immortality) - Tremere Reaper (Marginal)<ul><li>Immortality</li> <li>Soul Thief (Person must offer their soul without hard leverage)</li> <li>Numen - Resurrection (Requires 7 Souls)<ul><li>Feeding Aspiration: Dissolving a soul for nourishment</li> <li>Bane: Not fulfilling Feeding Aspiration</li> </ul></li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div> This is how I handle Tremere in my setting. I should note I count Bloodlines, Legacies, Entitlements, Lodges as the Exclusive Minor Templates, all others can be taken by those that meet the prerequisites. Banes inflict its affect when the circumstance applies.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-19-2017, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T09:48:54-08:00","id":1034672,"title":"","content":"If it were me, I'd drop any connection to Disciplines or the physical power of the Kindred. The Tremere are interested in ultimate power, and the triflings of the Kindred pale in comparison to what they're after. Tremere are all about the soul.<br /> <br /> I'd treat the Tremere almost as a special sort of Mad, except that, instead of Tulpae, they feed on souls. Give them some special insights into souls that other Mages would kill for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:08:29-08:00","id":1034685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034672#post1034672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it were me, I'd drop any connection to Disciplines or the physical power of the Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>This re-imagining does play towards both origin stories of the Tremere - vampires are able to become one just like Mages are, so dropping all of their abilities would be problematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T12:00:11-08:00","id":1034761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034685#post1034685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This re-imagining does play towards both origin stories of the Tremere - vampires are able to become one just like Mages are, so dropping all of their abilities would be problematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does one become Tremere? Embrace is out, and I can't see them Awakening that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T12:30:17-08:00","id":1034782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034761#post1034761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does one become Tremere? Embrace is out, and I can't see them Awakening that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The methods I have so far (still tentative) are:<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Becoming Tremere</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Characters become Tremere through any of the following methods:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf A Mage is resurrected, soulless, by a separate effect during the same scene an Embrace was attempted on them.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf A vampire fully diablerizes the soul of a Mage as part of a powerful blood sorcery ritual.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Other circumstances - such as a Strix utilizing Synthesis on one of the Awakened, can also lead to the creation of one of the Tremere.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T12:47:20-08:00","id":1034788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034685#post1034685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This re-imagining does play towards both origin stories of the Tremere - vampires are able to become one just like Mages are, so dropping all of their abilities would be problematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>My instinctive response from that is to step away, I'm afraid, but I wish you all the best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:13:35-08:00","id":1034813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034782#post1034782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The methods I have so far (still tentative) are:<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Becoming Tremere</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Characters become Tremere through any of the following methods:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf A Mage is resurrected, soulless, by a separate effect during the same scene an Embrace was attempted on them.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf A vampire fully diablerizes the soul of a Mage as part of a powerful blood sorcery ritual.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Other circumstances - such as a Strix utilizing Synthesis on one of the Awakened, can also lead to the creation of one of the Tremere.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>What about attempting to replace their soul using a Kindred soul (via Death 5 spell)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:18:34-08:00","id":1034819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034813#post1034813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about attempting to replace their soul using a Kindred soul (via Death 5 spell)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason I went with the resurrection angle is that all Resurrection powers in 2E lead to soullessness or similar strangeness (AFAIK), which acts as a convenient metaphysical excuse. It also operates under the assumption that the only reason Mages can't be embraced is because they can't be brought back by the Beast after it takes place. So if something else brings them back...<br /> <br /> That said, these methods are tuned for 'Tremere are extremely rare outside of intentional attempts to create them, mostly by other Tremere'. If you want them to be more common, or more easily created, I'd adjust creation methods accordingly. Replacing one's soul with a Vampires would be a great example there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T14:40:58-08:00","id":1034869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1034819#post1034819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason I went with the resurrection angle is that all Resurrection powers in 2E lead to soullessness or similar strangeness (AFAIK), which acts as a convenient metaphysical excuse. It also operates under the assumption that the only reason Mages can't be embraced is because they can't be brought back by the Beast after it takes place. So if something else brings them back...<br /> <br /> That said, these methods are tuned for 'Tremere are extremely rare outside of intentional attempts to create them, mostly by other Tremere'. If you want them to be more common, or more easily created, I'd adjust creation methods accordingly. Replacing one's soul with a Vampires would be a great example there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, this just got me thinking about my version. The Resurrect Numen would only resurrect vampires or mages without minor templates which then adds the Tremere Reaper Minor Template.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-19-2017, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T06:58:56-08:00","id":1035197,"title":"","content":"Weird thought process:<br /> Could a Tremere <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Use Death to create Ghost A from Person A.</li> <li>Steal Person A's Soul.</li> <li>Use Death to amp up Ghost A to the point it has the Claim Manifestation.</li> <li>Use Death to compel Ghost A to Claim Person A (easier, since A is soulless).</li> <li>Person A is now a Claimed (by their own Ghost, no less).</li> </ol><br /> Would the status of being Claimed hold off Soullessness? Yeah, there are bound to be side-effects, but would they be better than outright soullessness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T08:16:17-08:00","id":1035229,"title":"","content":"I don't see why anyone with Death couldn't do that. I wouldn't call them better off than soulless though. At best it probably would look like someone trapped in the Soulless Condition, but not suffering degeneration into the subsequent Conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T08:33:52-08:00","id":1035237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1035229#post1035229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why anyone with Death couldn't do that. I wouldn't call them better off than soulless though. At best it probably would look like someone trapped in the Soulless Condition, but not suffering degeneration into the subsequent Conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, nothing about it requires Tremere. I was thinking one of them might use such a method to mitigate their negative consequences.<br /> <br /> Again, not an ideal solution, but surely better than leaving others broken Thralls. Right? (Or, such would likely be said Tremere's desperate justifications)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T08:36:56-08:00","id":1035241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1035237#post1035237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, nothing about it requires Tremere. I was thinking one of them might use such a method to mitigate their negative consequences.<br /> <br /> Again, not an ideal solution, but surely better than leaving others broken Thralls. Right? (Or, such would likely be said Tremere's desperate justifications)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hardly cost effective requiring multiple spells, including Mastery of Death, taking up spell control or lots of XP from safely relinquished spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T08:52:12-08:00","id":1035250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1035241#post1035241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's hardly cost effective requiring multiple spells, including Mastery of Death, taking up spell control or lots of XP from safely relinquished spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mana Cost vs shreds of self-respect and conscience. As for spell control, if the mage get it down to a single spell that needs to be maintained, and establishes a halfway decent connection with the &quot;target&quot; (as opposed to a blind soul-mugging), they might have the now-sleepwalker-by-default (see: Claimed) hold the spell for them.<br /> <hr /><br /> EDIT: Yes, the hurdles you illustrated means that said hypothetical Tremere would have to be very committed to this method of maybe-mitigation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T09:59:52-08:00","id":1035289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1035197#post1035197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird thought process:<br /> Could a Tremere<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Use Death to create Ghost A from Person A.</li> <li>Steal Person A's Soul.</li> <li>Use Death to amp up Ghost A to the point it has the Claim Manifestation.</li> <li>Use Death to compel Ghost A to Claim Person A (easier, since A is soulless).</li> <li>Person A is now a Claimed (by their own Ghost, no less).</li> </ol><br /> Would the status of being Claimed hold off Soullessness? Yeah, there are bound to be side-effects, but would they be better than outright soullessness?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not so much a weird thought process as a kind of roundabout and thematically dubious means of doing something that you could as readily do by just binding the created ghost into its template person with Revenant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T10:12:34-08:00","id":1035295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1035289#post1035289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not so much a weird thought process as a kind of roundabout and thematically dubious means of doing something that you could as readily do by just binding the created ghost into its template person with Revenant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgot that. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T11:00:17-08:00","id":1035315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1035197#post1035197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the status of being Claimed hold off Soullessness? Yeah, there are bound to be side-effects, but would they be better than outright soullessness?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nothing in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1035242-claimed-vampire?p=1035301#post1035301\">Claimed Condition</a> says anything about helping the Soulless Condition<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>SOULLESS (PERSISTENT) CONDITION</b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CofD Pg 290</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A creature or phenomenon has stripped the character of her soul. Without a soul, she can\u2019t attempt abjuration, warding, or binding. She is also more susceptible to possession \u2014 any dice pools to resist being taken over or possessed by another entity are at a -2 dice penalty. The effects on Integrity and Willpower, though, are more severe. For as long as she has this Condition, she does not regain Willpower through surrender or rest, and her use of Virtue and Vice is reversed. She may regain one Willpower point per scene by fulfilling her Virtue, and regains full Willpower once per chapter by fulfilling her Vice. Regaining Willpower through Vice, though, is now a breaking point with a -5 penalty unless the character has reached Integrity 1.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Gain a beat whenever the character loses Integrity because she indulged her Vice.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>This Condition is only resolved if <u>the character r<i>egains</i> their soul</u>.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> and having a Ghost that was your soul Claim your body may, or may not counts as &quot;regaining&quot; your Soul based on Storyteller interpretation. (underlined and italics emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> Also <b>Forge Empty Wolf </b>(<b>WtF 2nd Ed</b> Pg 219) Servant creating power of some idigam is very similar to what you purposed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-20-2017, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:43:39-08:00","id":1035426,"title":"","content":"Ghosts aren't souls <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3279\" data-vbnamecard=\"3279\">Pale_Crusader</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:47:07-08:00","id":1035465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1035426#post1035426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts aren't souls <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3279\" data-vbnamecard=\"3279\">Pale_Crusader</a></div> </div> </div> </div>So you are absolutely right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1035197#post1035197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Use Death to create Ghost A from Person A.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got it into my head that the Ghost created was somehow made from Person A's Soul. but then this couldn't be the next step:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere?p=1035197#post1035197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Steal Person A's Soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am noticing Sever Soul doesn't make Ghosts but severs Souls, so <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> must mean Create Ghost with the Making Practice. Sorry for being confused. In that case tit is really clear that it wouldn't resolve the Soulless Condition. I'd notice the Claimed created via the suggested protocol would be a horrific monstrous version of itself. Don't forget Claimed physically mutate because of the merging (in this case, to an exaggerated version of themselves, I'd suspect) gaining Attribute boosts based on Power/Finesse/Resistance, along with the Bane and Ban of the Ephemeral Entity. Not sure what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> meant by &quot;Ghost A <i>from</i> Person A&quot;, maybe he meant &quot;<i>based on</i>&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-20-2017, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T05:18:48-08:00","id":1036551,"title":"","content":"I think I've worked out most of the kinks. A fun bit was that vampires have no way to heal Resistant damage as written. This not only effects Tremere, but Kindred attacked via Devour the Slain.<br /> <br /> I'm going with the ruling that, like aggravated damage, it's something they can only heal during Daysleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T01:51:02-08:00","id":1037087,"title":"","content":"Very interested in th